Cool. The main difference I can see between myself and the other guy who
was writing about learning Dvorak is that he seemed bent on destroying his
QWERTY skills to the point of actually forcing himself to type with two
fingers in QWERTY to hamper his fluency. And he was using total immersion
learning. I, on the other hand, have no reservations about using BOTH
Dvorak AND QWERTY during the course of the day, so I consider that I've
had a lot of time to get used to the differences between the layouts.
